IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc7-s183-base`

-- ccc7-s183-definitions.l4 -- section 183 (the definitions of Part VI, "In this Part,") except "offence" (ccc7-s183-offence.l4),
-- and section 183.1 (consent to interception), of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text. The French equivalents in
-- parentheses at the end of a defined term are quoted with the line, not encoded.
-- Every definition answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE (within the term), JUST FALSE (the text says no: "means" and the case is outside it),
-- NOTHING (not covered: "includes", an undefined term, silence). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- "means ... and includes ..." is read as closed (the means part plus the listed extension), as the keel reads it (keel fork F2).

§ `Section 183 -- Definitions ("In this Part,")`

-- authorization means an authorization to intercept a private communication given under subsection 184.2(3), section 186 or subsection 188(2).
-- Plain gloss: the permission a judge gives to listen in; only those three kinds of order are "authorizations" in this Part.
DECLARE `s 183 kind of instrument` IS ONE OF
    `s 183 an instrument given under subsection 184.2(3)`
    `s 183 an instrument given under section 186`
    `s 183 an instrument given under subsection 188(2)`
    `s 183 an instrument given under no other provision named`

-- src:3524 | authorization means an authorization to intercept a private communication given under subsection 184.2(3), section 186 or subsection 188(2); (autorisation)
@ref Criminal Code s 183 "authorization" (src:3524-3524)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 183 kind of instrument`
      `it is an authorization to intercept a private communication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183 authorization` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 183 an instrument given under subsection 184.2(3)` THEN `the instrument authorizes interception`
    WHEN `s 183 an instrument given under section 186` THEN `the instrument authorizes interception`
    WHEN `s 183 an instrument given under subsection 188(2)` THEN `the instrument authorizes interception`
    WHEN `s 183 an instrument given under no other provision named` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "authorization means an authorization to intercept a private communication given under"
    WHERE
        `the instrument authorizes interception` MEANS
            IF `it is an authorization to intercept a private communication`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "authorization means an authorization to intercept a private communication"

-- electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device means any device or apparatus that is used or is capable of being used to intercept a private communication,
-- but does not include a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing.
-- Plain gloss: a bug, recorder, tap or anything that can be used to listen in; an ordinary hearing aid does not count.
-- src:3525 | electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device means any device or apparatus that is used or is capable of being used to intercept a private communication, but does not include a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing; (dispositif électromagnétique, acoustique, mécanique ou autre)
@ref Criminal Code s 183 "electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device" (src:3525-3525)
GIVEN `it is a device or apparatus that is used or is capable of being used to intercept a private communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183 electro-magnetic, acoustic, mechanical or other device` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include a hearing aid used to correct subnormal hearing of the user to not better than normal hearing"
        IF `it is a device or apparatus that is used or is capable of being used to intercept a private communication`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any device or apparatus that is used or is capable of being used to intercept a private communication"

-- intercept includes listen to, record or acquire a communication or acquire the substance, meaning or purport thereof.
-- Plain gloss: listening to, recording or getting a communication, or getting what it says or means, is intercepting; the list is open ("includes").
DECLARE `s 183 act on a communication` IS ONE OF
    `s 183 listening to a communication`
    `s 183 recording a communication`
    `s 183 acquiring a communication`
    `s 183 acquiring the substance, meaning or purport of a communication`
    `s 183 an act that is none of those`

-- src:3526 | intercept includes listen to, record or acquire a communication or acquire the substance, meaning or purport thereof; (intercepter)
@ref Criminal Code s 183 "intercept" (src:3526-3526)
GIVEN act IS A `s 183 act on a communication`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183 intercept` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 183 listening to a communication` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 183 recording a communication` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 183 acquiring a communication` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 183 acquiring the substance, meaning or purport of a communication` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 183 an act that is none of those` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "intercept includes"

-- police officer means any officer, constable or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace.
-- Plain gloss: anyone employed to keep the public peace; note that this Part has its own "police officer", apart from the section 2 "peace officer".
-- src:3739 | police officer means any officer, constable or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace; (policier)
@ref Criminal Code s 183 "police officer" (src:3739-3739)
GIVEN `the person is an officer, constable or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183 police officer` MEANS
    IF `the person is an officer, constable or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "police officer means any officer, constable or other person employed for the preservation and maintenance of the public peace"

-- private communication means any oral communication, or any telecommunication, that is made by an originator who is in Canada or is intended by the originator to be received
-- by a person who is in Canada and that is made under circumstances in which it is reasonable for the originator to expect that it will not be intercepted by any person other than the
-- person intended by the originator to receive it, and includes any radio-based telephone communication that is treated electronically or otherwise for the purpose of preventing
-- intelligible reception by any person other than the person intended by the originator to receive it.
-- Plain gloss: a call, message or conversation that the speaker could reasonably expect to stay private, made by someone in Canada or meant for someone in Canada.
-- src:3740 | private communication means any oral communication, or any telecommunication, that is made by an originator who is in Canada or is intended by the originator to be received by a person who is in Canada and that is made under circumstances in which it is reasonable for the originator to expect that it will not be intercepted by any person other than the person intended by the originator to receive it, and includes any radio-based telephone communication that is treated electronically or otherwise for the purpose of preventing intelligible reception by any person other than the person intended by the originator to receive it; (communication privée)
@ref Criminal Code s 183 "private communication" (src:3740-3740)
GIVEN `it is an oral communication, or a telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made by an originator who is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is intended by the originator to be received by a person who is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made under circumstances in which it is reasonable for the originator to expect that it will not be intercepted by any person other than the person intended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a radio-based telephone communication, by s 183` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is treated electronically or otherwise for the purpose of preventing intelligible reception by any person other than the person intended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183 private communication` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the means part` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the includes part` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the means part` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`the includes part` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "private communication means any oral communication, or any telecommunication"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the telephone communication is a radio-based telephone communication is for the definition of that term, which is itself not covered
    WHERE
        `the means part` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued all of`
                (LIST
                    `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `it is an oral communication, or a telecommunication`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer`
                        (`it is made by an originator who is in Canada` OR `it is intended by the originator to be received by a person who is in Canada`)
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `it is made under circumstances in which it is reasonable for the originator to expect that it will not be intercepted by any person other than the person intended`)
        `the includes part` MEANS
            `s 183 three-valued all of`
                (LIST
                    `it is a radio-based telephone communication, by s 183`
                    , `s 183 as a three-valued answer` `it is treated electronically or otherwise for the purpose of preventing intelligible reception by any person other than the person intended`)

-- public switched telephone network means a telecommunication facility the primary purpose of which is to provide a land line-based telephone service to the public for compensation.
-- Plain gloss: the ordinary wired telephone system that the public pays to use.
-- src:3741 | public switched telephone network means a telecommunication facility the primary purpose of which is to provide a land line-based telephone service to the public for compensation; (réseau téléphonique public commuté)
@ref Criminal Code s 183 "public switched telephone network" (src:3741-3741)
GIVEN `it is a telecommunication facility` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its primary purpose is to provide a land line-based telephone service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is provided to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is provided for compensation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183 public switched telephone network` MEANS
    IF `it is a telecommunication facility` AND `its primary purpose is to provide a land line-based telephone service` AND `the service is provided to the public` AND `the service is provided for compensation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "public switched telephone network means a telecommunication facility the primary purpose of which is to provide a land line-based telephone service to the public for compensation"

-- radio-based telephone communication means any radiocommunication within the meaning of the Radiocommunication Act that is made over apparatus that is used primarily for connection to a public switched telephone network.
-- "radiocommunication" is the Radiocommunication Act's term, which is not among the sources: asked as a fact. The network is the answer of `s 183 public switched telephone network`.
-- src:3742 | radio-based telephone communication means any radiocommunication within the meaning of the Radiocommunication Act that is made over apparatus that is used primarily for connection to a public switched telephone network; (communication radiotéléphonique)
@ref Criminal Code s 183 "radio-based telephone communication" (src:3742-3742)
GIVEN `it is a radiocommunication within the meaning of the Radiocommunication Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made over apparatus that is used primarily for connection to a network` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the network is a public switched telephone network, by s 183` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183 radio-based telephone communication` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is a radiocommunication within the meaning of the Radiocommunication Act`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "radio-based telephone communication means any radiocommunication within the meaning of the Radiocommunication Act"
        IF NOT `it is made over apparatus that is used primarily for connection to a network`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that is made over apparatus that is used primarily for connection to a public switched telephone network"
        OTHERWISE `the network is a public switched telephone network, by s 183`   -- JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE ("means"); NOTHING only when s 183 "public switched telephone network" is itself not covered

-- sell includes offer for sale, expose for sale, have in possession for sale or distribute or advertise for sale.
-- Plain gloss: selling is wider than a completed sale; the list is open ("includes"). FORK (F4): "have in possession for sale or distribute or advertise for sale" can be read as five acts
-- (offer for sale; expose for sale; have in possession for sale; distribute; advertise for sale) or as four ("have in possession for sale or distribute" being one act, possession for sale or for distribution).
DECLARE `s 183 act of selling` IS ONE OF
    `s 183 offering for sale`
    `s 183 exposing for sale`
    `s 183 having in possession for sale`
    `s 183 distributing`
    `s 183 advertising for sale`
    `s 183 an act that is none of those named`

-- src:3743 | sell includes offer for sale, expose for sale, have in possession for sale or distribute or advertise for sale; (vendre)
@ref Criminal Code s 183 "sell" (src:3743-3743)
GIVEN act IS A `s 183 act of selling`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183 sell` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 183 offering for sale` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 183 exposing for sale` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 183 having in possession for sale` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 183 distributing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 183 advertising for sale` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 183 an act that is none of those named` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "sell includes"

-- solicitor means, in the Province of Quebec, an advocate or a notary and, in any other province, a barrister or solicitor.
-- Plain gloss: the kind of lawyer depends on the province. FORK (F5): the three territories are neither "the Province of Quebec" nor "any other province": the definition is silent, so NOTHING.
DECLARE `s 183 kind of legal practitioner` IS ONE OF
    `s 183 an advocate`
    `s 183 a notary`
    `s 183 a barrister`
    `s 183 a solicitor`
    `s 183 a practitioner of none of those kinds`

-- src:3744 | solicitor means, in the Province of Quebec, an advocate or a notary and, in any other province, a barrister or solicitor. (avocat)
@ref Criminal Code s 183 "solicitor" (src:3744-3744)
GIVEN province IS A `Province or territory`
      practitioner IS A `s 183 kind of legal practitioner`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183 solicitor` MEANS
    CONSIDER province
    WHEN Quebec THEN `in the Province of Quebec`
    WHEN Yukon THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a territory is not "the Province of Quebec" nor "any other province"
    WHEN `Northwest Territories` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a territory is not "the Province of Quebec" nor "any other province"
    WHEN Nunavut THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a territory is not "the Province of Quebec" nor "any other province"
    OTHERWISE `in any other province`
    WHERE
        `in the Province of Quebec` MEANS
            CONSIDER practitioner
            WHEN `s 183 an advocate` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `s 183 a notary` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `s 183 a barrister` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "solicitor means, in the Province of Quebec, an advocate or a notary"
            WHEN `s 183 a solicitor` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "solicitor means, in the Province of Quebec, an advocate or a notary"
            WHEN `s 183 a practitioner of none of those kinds` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "solicitor means, in the Province of Quebec, an advocate or a notary"
        `in any other province` MEANS
            CONSIDER practitioner
            WHEN `s 183 a barrister` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `s 183 a solicitor` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `s 183 an advocate` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any other province, a barrister or solicitor"
            WHEN `s 183 a notary` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any other province, a barrister or solicitor"
            WHEN `s 183 a practitioner of none of those kinds` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any other province, a barrister or solicitor"

§ `Section 183.1 -- Consent to interception`

-- 183.1 Where a private communication is originated by more than one person or is intended by the originator thereof to be received by more than one person, a consent to the interception thereof
-- by any one of those persons is sufficient consent for the purposes of any provision of this Part.
-- Plain gloss: if several people are on the call, the consent of any one of them is enough. The function is named for what the SECTION does (it makes one person's consent sufficient),
-- not for whether the interception is lawful, which other sections decide. FORK (F6): "Where" failing is JUST FALSE (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)); a consent by someone who is not one of those persons
-- is outside the limit of the grant ("by any one of those persons") and is NOTHING.
-- src:3745 | Consent to interception
-- src:3746 | 183.1 Where a private communication is originated by more than one person or is intended by the originator thereof to be received by more than one person, a consent to the interception thereof by any one of those persons is sufficient consent for the purposes of any provision of this Part.
@ref Criminal Code s 183.1 (src:3745-3746)
GIVEN `the communication is originated by more than one person or is intended by the originator to be received by more than one person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent to the interception was given by one of those persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 183.1 the section makes one person's consent sufficient consent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the communication is originated by more than one person or is intended by the originator to be received by more than one person`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a private communication is originated by more than one person or is intended by the originator thereof to be received by more than one person"
        IF `the consent to the interception was given by one of those persons`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a consent to the interception thereof by any one of those persons is sufficient consent"
